-- title:
--   Uniform index bound for ideals of a reduced ℤ-order
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be a commutative ring which is reduced (it has no nonzero nilpotent elements) and whose underlying additive group is a finitely generated free $\mathbb{Z}$-module. The assertion is that there exists a natural number $c$ with $c>0$ such that for every natural number $n \neq 0$ and every ideal $J$ of $B$ containing the image of $n$ in $B$, one has
--   $$\#(B/J) \;\le\; c \cdot \#\{\, x \in B/nB \;:\; a\,x = 0 \text{ for all } a \in J \,\},$$
--   where $B/nB$ is the quotient of $B$ by the ideal generated by $(n : B)$, the right-hand set is the $B$-submodule of $B/nB$ annihilated by the set of all elements of $J$, and both cardinalities are understood as `Nat.card` (so a value $0$ for infinite sets). The constant $c$ is obtained before, and hence is independent of, both $n$ and $J$; it depends only on $B$.
--
--   This is the bound on the Gorenstein defect of a reduced $\mathbb{Z}$-order: the index of an ideal $J \ni n$ is controlled, uniformly in $n$ and $J$, by the number of classes modulo $n$ killed by $J$ (for a Gorenstein order the two counts agree). It is the commutative-algebra input, applied to Hecke algebras acting on lattices of cusp forms, for [`ModularCurve.exists_sq_natCard_heckeLatticeAlgebra_quotient_le_natCard_torsionBySet_mul_pow`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_sq_natCard_heckeLatticeAlgebra_quotient_le_natCard_torsionBySet_mul_pow), which converts counts of $J$-torsion classes modulo $n$ into a lower bound for $\#(B/J)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Ideal_exists_forall_natCard_quotient_le_mul_natCard_torsionBySet_of_isReduced.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
